        "id": 3511933,
        "postDate": "2026-08-12T10:54:21.033Z",
        "rawMarkdown": "I had similar experience with the CSIRO Biomass competition... My hypothesis is that the gram anchoring that makes DinoV3 so powerful is only helpful with massive datasets and long training, which we do not have. The pretrained weights are also better from v3, but if finetuning is needed, these are lost.\n",
        "content": "<p>I had similar experience with the CSIRO Biomass competition… My hypothesis is that the gram anchoring that makes DinoV3 so powerful is only helpful with massive datasets and long training, which we do not have. The pretrained weights are also better from v3, but if finetuning is needed, these are lost.</p>",
